{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["<b>A lion's whelp.</b> He prophesied concerning David — at first a גּוּר, 'when Saul was king over us, you were the one who led out and brought in Israel' (II Samuel 5) — and ultimately an אַרְיֵה, when they made him king over them. And this is what Onkelos rendered: שִׁלְטוֹן יְהֵא בְּשֵׁרוּיָא — 'dominion shall be at its beginning.'" "<b>From the prey.</b> From that of which I suspected you — in 'a vicious beast has torn him apart' — and this is Judah, who is compared to a lion." "<b>You have gone up, my son.</b> You elevated yourself and said, 'What profit...' and so on, and likewise in the episode of Tamar, whom you condemned — he admitted, 'She is more righteous than I.' Therefore <b>he crouched, he lay down</b> and so on. In the days of Solomon, 'every man under his vine' and so on (I Kings 5)."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 49, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:04:05.115377692Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}